{
  "result": "If I could change one thing, it wouldn't be a law or a technology. It would be smaller, and more upstream.\n\nI'd remove the distance.\n\nNot intellectually \u2014 people already *know* other people suffer. I mean the felt distance that lets us act like they don't. The ability to ignore someone, judge them, cheat them, drop a bomb on them, without it ever really landing in our own body.\n\nIf everyone, even just for a few seconds, actually experienced what it's like to be the person on the other side of their indifference \u2014 not as an idea, but as a lived moment \u2014 I think most of the worst stuff becomes much harder to do.\n\nPeople would still argue. They'd still disagree, compete, want different things. But they'd have a much harder time telling themselves the other side isn't fully real.\n\nThat's the one I'd choose.",
